# Milestone 010: Move Ristretto to Otter v2 - Completed

## Summary
Replaced `github.com/dgraph-io/ristretto/v2` with `github.com/maypok86/otter/v2` (v2.3.0) throughout the cache layer.

## Changes Made

### internal/cache/blocklist.go
- Replaced ristretto.Cache[string, time.Time] + sync.Map with otter.Cache[string, *blocklistEntryData]
- Eliminated secondary sync.Map index — otter's native `cache.All()` iteration replaces it
- Used `ExpiryCreatingFunc` for variable per-entry TTLs (reads expiresAt from the stored value)
- Used `OnDeletion` with `WasEvicted()` for eviction metrics
- Replaced: Get→GetIfPresent, SetWithTTL→Set, Del→Invalidate, Wait→(removed, writes are sync), Close→StopAllGoroutines
- Count() now uses EstimatedSize(), Clear() uses InvalidateAll()
- Removed Metrics() method that returned *ristretto.Metrics (was unused externally)

### internal/cache/accounting.go
- Replaced ristretto.Cache[string, *atomic.Int64] with otter.Cache[string, *atomic.Int64]
- Used `ExpiryCreating` for uniform window TTL across all entries
- Same API replacements as blocklist (GetIfPresent, Set, Invalidate, StopAllGoroutines)
- Removed Metrics() method that returned *ristretto.Metrics (was unused externally)

### go.mod
- Added: github.com/maypok86/otter/v2 v2.3.0
- Removed: github.com/dgraph-io/ristretto/v2 v2.4.0

## Test Results
- All 40 cache tests pass with -race flag
- All other packages (accounting, api, config, grpc, metrics, model, ratelimit) pass
- Zero lint issues
- Pre-existing membership test race (unrelated to this change) remains

## Key Design Decisions
- S3-FIFO eviction policy (otter default) replaces TinyLFU (ristretto)
- Weight-based eviction via MaximumWeight + Weigher (100 bytes per entry) preserves existing cost model
- ExpiryCreatingFunc allows variable TTLs without needing Set + SetExpiresAfter two-step
- No secondary index needed — otter.All() provides thread-safe iteration natively
